1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,460
Have you ever wondered why

2
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:03,120
FC Barcelona's crest looks the

3
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:03,760
way it does?

4
00:00:04,160 --> 00:00:05,220
Why does it contain the

5
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:06,440
red and yellow stripes of

6
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:06,840
Catalonia?

7
00:00:07,900 --> 00:00:09,400
Why is there a cross

8
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:11,460
that looks almost identical

9
00:00:11,460 --> 00:00:12,840
to the flag of England?

10
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,360
And what does the ancient

11
00:00:14,360 --> 00:00:16,540
kingdom of Aragon have to

12
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:18,080
do with one of football's

13
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,640
most recognizable symbols?

14
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:20,720
Well,

15
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:23,040
the story behind Barcelona's badge

16
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,080
goes much further back than

17
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:25,900
football itself.

18
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:27,400
Let's start with the red

19
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,680
and yellow stripes at the

20
00:00:28,680 --> 00:00:29,460
top of the crest.

21
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,240
These stripes

22
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,100
represent the Senyera,

23
00:00:33,460 --> 00:00:34,900
the traditional flag of Catalonia.

24
00:00:35,380 --> 00:00:36,420
It consists of

25
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:38,080
four red stripes on a

26
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,580
golden background and is one

27
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:40,940
of the oldest and most

28
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:43,120
recognizable symbols of Catalan

29
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:44,040
identity.

30
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:46,360
But its history goes even

31
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:47,140
further back.

32
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:48,740
The four red stripes are

33
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:50,280
historically associated with the

34
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:51,580
House of Barcelona and the

35
00:00:51,580 --> 00:00:53,140
wider Crown of Aragon,

36
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,340
a medieval political union that

37
00:00:55,340 --> 00:00:56,700
became one of the most

38
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,320
influential powers in the

39
00:00:58,320 --> 00:00:59,160
Western Mediterranean.

40
00:00:59,160 --> 00:01:00,880
The Crown of Aragon was

41
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:02,360
not simply the modern region

42
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:02,920
of Aragon.

43
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:04,480
It was a composite monarchy

44
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:06,120
whose territories included

45
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,980
Aragon, Catalonia, Valencia

46
00:01:07,980 --> 00:01:09,920
and, at different periods, other

47
00:01:09,920 --> 00:01:11,080
Mediterranean lands.

48
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:12,320
This is why the same

49
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:14,420
four-stripe heraldic design appears

50
00:01:14,420 --> 00:01:16,540
in different historical symbols across

51
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:17,160
the region.

52
00:01:17,900 --> 00:01:18,800
So when you look at

53
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:20,260
those red and yellow stripes

54
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:21,440
on Barcelona's crest,

55
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:23,180
you're not just looking at

56
00:01:23,180 --> 00:01:24,080
club colors.

57
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:25,700
You're looking at a symbol

58
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,500
connected to centuries of regional

59
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,020
history.

60
00:01:28,020 --> 00:01:29,660
Now let's look at the

61
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,840
other symbol in the upper

62
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:31,800
part of the crest,

63
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:33,820
the red cross on a

64
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:34,480
white background.

65
00:01:34,920 --> 00:01:35,760
This is the cross of

66
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:36,240
St. George,

67
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,940
known in Catalonia as

68
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:38,620
Sant Jordi.

69
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:40,620
St. George has a particularly

70
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,440
important place in Catalan history

71
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:43,940
and cultural identity.

72
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:45,920
He is considered the patron

73
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:47,740
saint of Catalonia and his

74
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:49,460
cross is also featured in

75
00:01:49,460 --> 00:01:50,500
the coat of arms of

76
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,740
the city of Barcelona.

77
00:01:52,700 --> 00:01:53,300
Interestingly,

78
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:55,560
the same red cross on

79
00:01:55,560 --> 00:01:57,020
a white background is also

80
00:01:57,020 --> 00:01:58,680
the national flag of England.

81
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,640
That's why you might notice

82
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:02,260
a striking resemblance between the

83
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:02,480
two.

84
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,200
But this doesn't mean Barcelona

85
00:02:04,200 --> 00:02:05,960
borrowed its symbol from England.

86
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:08,700
Both traditions are connected

87
00:02:08,700 --> 00:02:10,160
to the much older European

88
00:02:10,160 --> 00:02:11,520
veneration of St. George.

89
00:02:11,940 --> 00:02:13,300
But how did this historical

90
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,480
symbol become part of

91
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:15,120
FC Barcelona?

92
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,740
When Joan Gamper founded the

93
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:19,180
club in 1899,

94
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:21,240
Barcelona initially used the

95
00:02:21,240 --> 00:02:22,180
coat of arms of the

96
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:23,980
city as its official badge.

97
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:26,120
This continued until 1910.

98
00:02:26,460 --> 00:02:27,760
As the club developed its

99
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:28,660
own identity,

100
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,620
its board decided that it

101
00:02:30,620 --> 00:02:32,000
needed a distinctive emblem.

102
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,140
The competition was organized to

103
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:34,980
find a new design.

104
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,760
The winning design established the

105
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,320
basic structure of the crest

106
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:39,560
we recognize today.

107
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:41,720
It brought together several different

108
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:42,100
elements.

109
00:02:42,640 --> 00:02:43,760
The cross of St. George,

110
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,320
the four red stripes of

111
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:47,220
the Catalan flag, the club's

112
00:02:47,220 --> 00:02:47,600
initials,

113
00:02:48,140 --> 00:02:49,560
its famous blue and garnet

114
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,200
colors and a football at

115
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:51,560
the bottom.

116
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,300
It was a clever design

117
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:55,140
because it represented two sides

118
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:56,300
of the club at once.

119
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,280
Its connection to Barcelona and

120
00:02:58,280 --> 00:03:00,340
Catalonia and its identity as

121
00:03:00,340 --> 00:03:01,440
a football institution.

122
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:03,340
Since then, the badge has

123
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:05,300
undergone several visual modifications,

124
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,740
but its essential historical elements

125
00:03:07,740 --> 00:03:08,360
have remained.

126
00:03:09,060 --> 00:03:10,940
And perhaps that's what makes

127
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:13,000
Barcelona's crest so interesting.

128
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:14,480
It isn't just a logo

129
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:16,320
designed to identify a football

130
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:16,700
team.

131
00:03:17,180 --> 00:03:18,940
It's a combination of history,

132
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:19,800
culture,

133
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,300
regional identity and the sporting

134
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:22,820
tradition.

135
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:24,980
Every time a Barcelona player

136
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:26,060
wears that badge,

137
00:03:26,540 --> 00:03:28,320
they're carrying symbols that existed

138
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,320
long before the club was

139
00:03:30,320 --> 00:03:30,800
founded.

140
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:32,700
And that's one reason why

141
00:03:32,700 --> 00:03:34,780
for so many supporters, Barça

142
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,880
has always represented something bigger

143
00:03:36,880 --> 00:03:37,620
than football.

144
00:03:38,480 --> 00:03:39,300
Més que un club.
